  "findings": [
    "Root visually reviewed all eight contact sheets: four walk phases, front/rear at10/20m for Elder and Woman_Young. Contacts use unscaled240x320 crops from native960px images at45-degree FOV.",
    "Overall silhouette and corrected garment lighting remain close to the accepted skeletal source in these sampled distance views. No obvious new exposed skin patches or collapsed limbs were observed.",
    "Coarser hem/mantle folds and trim differences remain visible at10m. Facial detail is softer, especially Woman_Young. Differences are less prominent at20m; this is not a universal LOD threshold or near-character approval.",
    "All528 normal frames and saved texture pixels verify. Elder independently sampled frame0 differs by up to6 unsigned16 codewords (0.010051 degrees); remaining Elder samples and all Woman samples are codeword-exact. The direction comparison gate remains0.02 degrees, while saved texture pixel equality is exact.",
    "No continuous animation, loop seam, facial morph, idle GPU, transition, runtime adoption, all-cast or performance acceptance. Further reduction and thousands-of-people testing remain open."
  ],
  "next": "Continuous loop and transition review, all-cast geometry reduction and runtime crowd performance before adoption.",
